{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Your righteousness</b> — Rabbi Moses said: 'Your righteousness' — people cannot grasp, for it is like the mountains of El. The correct interpretation: it is loftied in its knowledge like the mighty mountains of El, which a person cannot reach; and likewise the knowledge of Your judgments is like the great deep, which is deep, which a person cannot see." "And the meaning of <b>man and beast</b>: that He will judge every sentient being, in the manner of: 'and from the hand of every beast I will demand it' (Genesis 9:5)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "Resolved ר' משה as 'Rabbi Moses' (likely R. Moses Ibn Ezra or R. Moses Ha-Kohen, uncertain which)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:49.461915319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}